// ==WindhawkMod==
// @id              start-orb
// @name            Start Orb
// @description     Turns the Windows 11 Start button into an animated orb: pick a built-in orb from a menu, or use your own picture
// @version         1.1.0
// @author          frozt
// @github          https://github.com/Frozt-src
// @include         explorer.exe
// @architecture    x86-64
// @compilerOptions -lole32 -loleaut32 -lruntimeobject
// ==/WindhawkMod==

// ==WindhawkModReadme==
/*
# Start Orb

Puts an animated orb on the Windows 11 Start button.

![Five of the built-in orbs](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frozt-src/windhawk-mods/start-orb-assets/start-orb-preview.gif)

1. Pick an orb.
2. Pick a size.
3. Click "Save settings".

That is all. The orb appears straight away. Point at Start and an animated orb plays half again as fast;
hold the click and it plays backwards.

## Using your own picture

Set "Orb" to "Custom". In File Explorer, right-click your picture, choose "Copy as path", and paste
it into "Picture" under "Customize". PNG, JPG and GIF are supported, and an animated GIF plays.
Paths may use variables such as `%USERPROFILE%\Pictures\orb.png`.

A web address (`https://...`) works too. Explorer downloads it each time it starts or the mod reloads,
and retries once a minute if the download fails. A file on your PC needs no network access.
 If a picture can't be loaded, the normal Windows logo stays.

Two optional extras: a different picture while the pointer is on Start, and another while you click.

## Making your own animated orb

A GIF plays as it is, but it has no soft edges, so it only looks right on the bar colour it was made
for. Animated PNG and WebP files show only their first frame. For a smooth animated orb with soft
edges, use a sprite sheet: one PNG with every frame side by side in a single row. Type the number of
frames into "Animation frames" and the mod plays them.

It works alongside other taskbar mods, including Windows 11 Taskbar Styler: it does not use the
XAML diagnostics channel that only one mod can hold. If a Styler theme also restyles the Start
button, remove that part of the theme so the two do not draw over each other.

## How this differs from Start Button Replacer

[Start Button Replacer](https://windhawk.net/mods/start-button-replacer) is the better choice for a
custom icon with separate activated and dark-mode images or scale, tilt and fade effects. Start Orb is
made for animated orbs: sixteen are built in, so no image file is needed, and it plays sprite sheets,
which keep the soft, partly transparent edges a GIF cannot.
*/
// ==/WindhawkModReadme==

// ==WindhawkModSettings==
